    "findings": {
      "privacy": "Only authored folder, artist and track labels, authored peak values, D11's copy and the anonymous gesture handle remain. No status strip, notification, account, path or device identifier is visible.",
      "darkColours": "In dark the header Back arrow and title, and the retained deck title, subtitle and transport buttons, are drawn in the theme's light text colour on the dark surfaces, as on the accepted Search page. The first build's black-on-dark header and deck text are gone.",
      "separators": "The header rule and every row separator run continuously across the unfolded panel's right half and have the same colour inside the fold connector as beyond it, in both themes.",
      "rows": "Each row's switch sits at the trailing edge, aligned with the first line of its title, and every switch shows its authored position in both themes. At 200% text on the unfolded panel the titles wrap to two lines, and Resume where I left off leaves the single word off on its second line. On the cover at 200% that title stays on one line.",
      "scrolling": "At 100% text the whole column, closing sentence included, is visible on both panels. At 200% text it scrolls on both panels. At the start of the unfolded column the last supporting line of the third row sits under the gesture handle and the closing sentence is below the visible area; on the cover the closing sentence's fourth line runs under the gesture handle. At the end of the column on both panels the whole closing sentence sits clear above the handle.",
      "leftHalf": "With Settings open on the unfolded panel, the left half keeps the same folder browser and full deck as the accepted Search page, narrower than the closed player's browser, so fewer folder names fit per line. At 200% text its browser viewport ends partway through a line of names, as on the Search page.",
      "cover": "On the cover the page is one full-width destination with the same header. The Back arrow keeps its 24dp glyph while the title grows at 200% text, so the arrow reads smaller beside the title; the 48dp target is unchanged."
    }
  },
